cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use signals_methods in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "signals_methods: Weak-signal detection methods for sensemaking under uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  Four novel weak-signal detection methods introduced as part of a Doctor of
  Engineering praxis at Penn State. The Information Vacuum Index (IVI) measures
  structural imbalance between discourse and authoritative activity; Narrative
  Velocity Divergence (NVD) measures per-narrative ratios of narrative velocity
  to evidence velocity; the Source Independence Graph (SIG) produces independence
  scores and amplification ratios from a citation graph; Sensemaking Quality
  Metrics (SQM) evaluate the three signals against a ground-truth timeline.
type: software
